# ZCode 本地会话/计划产物
.zcode/

# Fork: sealed distribution artifacts are BUILD OUTPUT, not source.
# Upstream commits them so a fresh clone runs without a build; this fork does
# not, because (a) they are AES blobs whose bytes change on every regeneration
# (random IV) so a merge conflict in them is unmergeable, and (b) GitHub push
# protection rejects the sealed references bundle: some reference document
# quotes a real-looking cloud access key, which passes upstream's own history
# but blocks any NEW commit carrying the regenerated blob.
# Regenerate with scripts/install-local.ps1 (build -> seal -> pack) or
# scripts/sync-upstream.ps1 after every upstream merge.
packages/helmd/payload.dat
packages/helmd/references.dat
packages/helmd/presets/profiles.dat

# Profile manifest/lockfile backups written by install-local.ps1
.backup/

